      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The curves meet where \\( y^{2} = 4 y + 5 \\), at \\( y = 5 \\), and the region runs from the x-axis, \\( y = 0 \\), up to there. On that interval the line is to the right of the parabola.",
         "rule_named": "limits in y and the right-hand curve"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The area is \\( \\int_{0}^{5} \\left(\\left(4 y + 5\\right) - \\left(y^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,dy = \\frac{100}{3} \\).",
